{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792757893,"nonce":"iqctEM6EsgV5NYwDuURAECskxM4=","title":"Compile targetless HXML builds with the Run default","message":"Ashui/build.hxml is a shared compiler configuration with no output target. Build invoked it unchanged and Haxe returned success without enabling the HashLink backend or native staging. Run adds -hl and exposed a hlavi native download error that Build had missed. A minimal conditional #if hl typing-error fixture reproduces exit 0 for haxe build.hxml and exit 1 when -hl is added. Targetless Build should use the same HashLink default as Run without launching output. Explicit targets, multi-target builds and deliberate --no-output checking should retain their declared behavior. Keep this correction separate from the code-action provider architecture now in progress.","files":null}]}